Database migrations (Alembic). Run every command from backend/.

Apply all pending migrations (local, CI, production):
    uv run alembic upgrade head

After changing a model in app/models:
    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"
    review the new file in migrations/versions/, then commit it with the model change
    uv run alembic upgrade head

Useful:
    uv run alembic current         which revision the database is on
    uv run alembic history         all revisions
    uv run alembic check           fails if the models changed without a migration
    uv run alembic downgrade -1    undo the last migration
    uv run alembic upgrade head --sql > upgrade.sql   SQL to review or hand to a DBA

The database URL comes from HIBANAKO_DATABASE_URL (or .env), the same as the app.
The Docker image runs `alembic upgrade head` before starting the API. The worker never migrates.

New empty database:      uv run alembic upgrade head
Database created before migrations existed (tables already there, made by the old auto-create):
    make sure `uv run alembic check` against it reports no differences, then
    uv run alembic stamp 0176e29859fb
